# Build context for geobase.dockerfile only. BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore
# in place of .dockerignore when one exists, so this replaces the shared file rather
# than adding to it.
#
# Both dockerfiles build from the same context, and the application image serves
# potree/ (69 MB) and pc-gltf-viewer/ (118 MB) as static files at runtime, so the
# shared .dockerignore cannot drop them. The geo base reads one 1.5 KB script and
# would otherwise ship all 187 MB to the daemon on every build.
#
# Adding a COPY to geobase.dockerfile means re-including its source here, or the
# build fails on a missing file.
*
!scripts
